{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1325994-base-successes","id":1325994,"title":"Base successes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-19T08:21:38-07:00","id":1325994,"title":"Base successes","content":"In M20 table we have some examples of base successes for some effects. Even having them as guidelines, it might be hard to choose how much successes are needed in different effects. <br /> M20 also states that personal or perception effects require 1 success and affecting others require at least 2.<br /> Not counting the successes x2 we already habe established to damage/healing or the ones that have tables (like teleportation, etc.)<br /> <br /> Having said that, how much successes would you require to:<br /> <br /> -Make the mage able to fly<br /> -Turning the mage invisible<br /> -Levitate/telekinesis something (weight is limited by dots in Forces)<br /> <br /> Do you follow the 1 success for personal 2 for outside world rule?<br /> <br /> Also, I'd like yo know if in your games, the character knows when a spell is successful or not, considering it doesn't have a obvious visual effect. For example, shoukd the mage know that his spell to affect someone's mood failed right away?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T16:22:02-07:00","id":1326122,"title":"","content":"Flying: prob like 2-3 for regular forces flying, much more for using forces 4 to control so much wind you basically can hang glide somewhere or for if you use life to make wings<br /> Invis: same as above, more if you add correspondence to see out of it (iirc using forces 2 to bend light leaves you blinded)<br /> Levitate: depends on what they want to do with it tbh. Chucking it really far? Prob a bit more than just holding it in the air. Not sure how many I'd rule<br /> <br /> Me and my st use the 1 success for personal effects and anymore after that we add to duration .<br /> <br /> We don't have my character know when his magick fails, though seeing as he doesn't have mind he usually figured it out rather quickly when his matter rotes to transmutate stuff haven't worked, but I don't necessarily lean one way or the other. Maybe allow a perception+ awareness roll dc their willpower to see if they notice if you don't tell them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T09:19:02-07:00","id":1326284,"title":"","content":"Hm, using the personal 1 success rule, shouldn't the flying and invisibility spell need just 1 success as base?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T11:07:53-07:00","id":1326303,"title":"","content":"I only really consider the personal effects to be sensory/really small things. Invisibility usually effects just a small aoe (Enough to cover yourself) as opposed to your body (Unless you add Life 2 because M20 hates you, and even then I think invis/flying is too much for just 1 success. And even then I think you'd need 2 for it to last any time other than a turn)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}